          %h2#references References
          %p
            The notion of pasting in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            was introduced in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+B%C3%A9nabou"}> Jean Bénabou
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to bicategories
                %em Lecture Notes in Mathematics
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 47
            %li#Johnson1987
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Johnson"}> Michael Johnson
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Pasting Diagrams in
                    = succeed "-Categories" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %li#Johnson1989
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Johnson"}> Michael Johnson
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    The Combinatorics of
                    = succeed "-Categorical" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %li#Power1990
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Power"}> John Power
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A 2-Categorical Pasting Theorem
                %strong 129
                2 (1990) 439-445 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-8693(90)90229-H"}> doi:10.1016/0021-8693(90)90229-H
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Other notions of pasting presentations have been given by Street (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parity+complexes"}> parity complexes
            ) and by Steiner,
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Parity complexes
                = succeed ")" do
